// bisect: fusion/JIT bug (interp != jit)
// THE GUARD RIDE (aug13b hz0-fuzz divergence_000000): a select whose
// GUARD bottoms (m = MIN % -1 on the 4th tick) must hold its standing
// selection QUIET — the interp's Held keeps the guard's last good
// value on a bottom production and is_match re-matches against it
// (unwrap_or(false) only for a no-history phantom). The kernel's
// prologue masked the tainted payload to plain false, failing the arm
// and firing a phantom becoming-selected on the wildcard (count 3 vs
// 2). Fixed by wrapping the prologue guard through
// emit_scalar_taint_cache — an op-site ride; claim-refused contexts
// (callee-body loops) degrade to the unwrapped mask, the same
// documented residual as every other op-site there.
// interp: [0:1 1:2] / pre-fix jit: [0:1 1:2 4:3]
{let x = array::iter([i64:1, i64:2, i64:3, i64:-9223372036854775808]); let m = x % i64:-1; let a = select i64:0 {i64:0 if m == i64:0 => i64:1, _ => i64:2}; count(a)}
